    {
      "name": "pending",
      "description": "List what push would send from a GitHub folder: files added, modified and deleted since the last pull or push (each with baseState, the space revision holding the previous version: read the path with that revision to compare). Also lists files .gitignore excludes (notPushed; .gitignore applies only to files the repository does not hold, as in git), changes push refuses (refused: files in .github/workflows/), and unchanged files pull converted to UTF-8 (converted: GitHub keeps its UTF-16/UTF-32 copy unless the file is edited; some Windows files need UTF-16, such as PowerShell 5.1 scripts with non-ASCII text and .reg files). upToDate means nothing to push; oldestChange says when the oldest pending change was written. Pass state as ifInState to push to send exactly what you checked. Read access is enough. Errors: conflict (not pulled yet).",
      "annotations": {
        "readOnlyHint": true,
